    {
      "id": 380937,
      "category": "researcher",
      "content": "The PoC link was as follows - \n\n```\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/mynetwork/send-invite/<USERNAME>/?lipi=urn:li:page:email_email_pymk_02;3MPU3ZpvSH6FxK37sN6PTA==&midSig=1H88TLaeqmRWI1&midToken=AQGOWzyQBc3Qug&trkEmail=eml-email_pymk_02-pymkCard-0-cta-null-h3akrx~lguw0uex~xs-null-null&trk=eml-email_pymk_02-pymkCard-0-cta&_sig=0y-j3QtmmmRWI1\n```\n\nHere the `<username>` is the Public Profile URL name. It was possible to make any user send connection invites to ourselves by simply providing them with the above crafted link. ",
      "updated_at": "2023-12-06T18:09:50.908Z",
